  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>stage_orders - validates the day's sales file and stages the good rows.

1. Read Sales: ${WORKSHOP_HOME}/data/sales_${SALES_DATE}.csv, header, comma, 7 fields (order_date as Date yyyy-MM-dd, unit_price as BigNumber).
2. Filter rows - a row is good when:
   customer_id IS NOT NULL AND product_id IS NOT NULL
   AND qty > 0 AND unit_price > 0 AND discount_pct between 0 and 100.
3. Good rows: Table output into stg_orders (truncated every run), then Group by (valid_rows = N(order_id)) and Write to log.
4. Bad rows: Rejected Sales writes out/rejected_${SALES_DATE}.csv (the audit trail), then Group by (rejected_rows) and Write to log.
   Both Group bys always give back a row, so a count of 0 is still logged.

Shipped data: 40 rows read, 37 staged, 3 rejected (missing customer or product).</note>
      <xloc>64</xloc>
      <yloc>48</yloc>
      <width>901</width>
      <heigth>206</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>0</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>0</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>0</fontcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorred>167</backgroundcolorred>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>224</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorblue>245</backgroundcolorblue>
      <bordercolorred>100</bordercolorred>
      <bordercolorgreen>100</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorblue>100</bordercolorblue>
      <drawshadow>Y</drawshadow>
    </notepad>
  </notepads>
